Observer of 5.2.1898 and Bromley Chronicle of 10.2.1898. The West Sussex
Gazette, Kentish Mercury, Evesham Standard and Bromley Chronicle versions
state that Black 'wins' in the final position given rather than White resigns.
The Evesham Standard and Bromley Chronicle versions do not name the players.
Black gave a pawn and two moves start. The game won the brilliancy prize 
(judged by Tarrasch) for the best game played at the Llandudno Tournament. 
(Brian Denman Collection)} 0-1

